e are investigating a suspected in-flight emergency on a Corfu flight. After the airport reopened, the airline said they believed the emergency code was a result of a technical malfunction.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Economy set for stronger growth, wine harvest hit by drought</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9519fea311329461a2c25289699a4fe049c9124f968a7d0b419d1e85888b0970</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-economy-set-for-stronger-growth-wine-harvest-hit-by-drought/live-79647092--5957f7bd3793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-economy-set-for-stronger-growth-wine-harvest-hit-by-drought/live-79647092?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economic outlook is looking a little brighter, with the International Monetary Fund almost doubling its growth forecast. However, Germany's winegrowers are facing another disappointing harvest. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db01490da9c6cfaa545406fdd6b27fda2b9b490f09b49ff88461335d621147f1</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz says Trump's Russia diesel deal 'out of question' for Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f4f84707b9081b4656c12397b542c40e4f0bb60c730d9534167fdf97b766cce</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-says-trump-s-russia-diesel-deal-out-of-question-for-europe/live-79636427--1a9438e4fa1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-says-trump-s-russia-diesel-deal-out-of-question-for-europe/live-79636427?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has said that Donald Trump's diesel deal with Russia would be "out of the question" for Germany and the EU. Meanwhile, the ruling coalition has been rocked by a major resignation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Frankfurt Book Fair: Rights lawyer Sands awarded peace prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0547b869403102467b3c7ca9ba8c71acb3ad4468ee550dd92b47e98bf2eacac</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T08:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/frankfurt-book-fair-rights-lawyer-sands-awarded-peace-prize/a-79637687--cf3106196409.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/frankfurt-book-fair-rights-lawyer-sands-awarded-peace-prize/a-79637687?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franco-British lawyer and author Philippe Sands was awarded the German Book Trade's Peace Prize this weekend. Accepting the award, Sands criticized Germany's "inappropriate silence" regarding Israel.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Bas quits as SPD co-chair amid coalition friction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9213b86b5e5f786be70f43d3fd4f5e0c3393c8d80f32e44429ef3946e2dedcf3</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T06:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-bas-quits-as-spd-co-chair-amid-coalition-friction/a-79636869--6c4bc88b7d1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-bas-quits-as-spd-co-chair-amid-coalition-friction/a-79636869?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bärbel Bas has resigned as labor minister and as co-leader of the Social Democrats as tension grows with Chancellor Merz's CDU.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf1cfc6e415451f9978b493d524e7f43e521d0113373e4bedef106297a276bc2</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:09:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Labor Minister's resignation puts a spotlight on cracks within the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aafe7c7de4442ef03e26b9e54960a71f6bc388ee8fe63a82115b2b381bc2e288</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823--1507ba6fa4a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the sudden resignation of Bärbel Bas as Labor Minister and co-chair of the Social Democratic Party, accusations are flying in Chancellor Merz's coalition government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af13874c120c14bf51f094fcf388cdc277a86dffa8124211fe47a4c27784240</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German 'lawfare': When lawsuits become a political weapon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb49495f1361a24382782994a0cb7b96fc405e00351b10699dffbd317dfe3305</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawfare-when-lawsuits-become-a-political-weapon/a-79615817--29d1d48e91a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawfare-when-lawsuits-become-a-political-weapon/a-79615817?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Left Party is suing two government ministers for accusing them of antisemitism, while Chancellor Friedrich Merz has been sued several times by various parties. Is German politics descending into "lawfare?"</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
